    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that an ISO {@link LocalDate} can be created from a {@link JulianDate} via {@link LocalDate#from(java.time.temporal.TemporalAccessor)}. <p> The Julian and ISO calendars differ only in their leap-year rule, and the two time-lines are aligned so that {@code 0001-01-01 (Julian)} equals {@code 0000-12-30 (ISO)}. The sample pairs below cover that alignment offset, Julian-only leap days (e.g. years 100, 1900) and the Gregorian-reform region."
   },
